  "candidate": "Scoped worker reuse across 1024-file batches; retained under cfg(test) in crates/riftri-storage/src/parallel/reuse_evaluation.rs, not used by release builds.",
  "baseline": "Whole-tree queue and previous draft's restarted-per-batch queue compared with the reusable-worker prototype in one release test binary.",
  "reproduce": "RIFTRI_CLONE_BENCH_DIRS=<1|32|128> RIFTRI_CLONE_BENCH_FILES=<8|64|128> RIFTRI_CLONE_BENCH_ROUNDS=12 cargo test --release -p riftri-storage --lib reports_batched_clone_comparison -- --ignored --nocapture",
  "method": "Twelve rounds per case, rotating all six execution-order permutations twice. 4 KiB files plus a readme and symlink; read-only source and owner-writable clones. Validation and per-call umask lookup timed equally. Contents, modes, names, symlinks and distinct file inodes verified after timing. No outliers removed. Medium repeated after large. Exploratory clone-stage measurements, not end-to-end creation, total RSS, or a cross-platform claim. A separate six-round medium verification run after isolating the prototype behind cfg(test) is also retained, not pooled with the twelve-round comparisons.",
  "assessment": "Reuse deterministically avoids worker recreation and keeps at most 1024 retained file jobs, but does not establish a consistent latency improvement. Medium results shift substantially between runs and the large reusable queue is slower than the unbounded baseline. Keep the prototype test-only and PR #660 draft.",
